# motion-budget

Public portfolio for Landon: a fictional product launch page plus CI that fails on motion or performance regressions. All copy, logos, and names are invented. No secrets, no real clients, no private-project code.

## Product

**Kiteframe** — fictional “CI for motion” profiler. Label it “Fictional product · portfolio demo.”

## Stack (do not add libraries without asking)

Next.js (latest stable, App Router), TypeScript strict, Tailwind, pnpm, GSAP + ScrollTrigger (sequenced timelines only), Playwright, Lighthouse CI (`@lhci/cli`), ESLint, GitHub Actions, Vercel. Use `next/font` and `next/image`.

## Motion (enforced by tests)

1. Animate only `transform` and `opacity`. Never `left`, `top`, `width`, `height`, `margin`, or `padding` (or those longhands).
2. `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` — no continuous or scroll-driven motion; short opacity fades are allowed.
3. CSS animations and CSS scroll-driven first. GSAP only for sequenced timelines; dynamically import it.
4. No CLS: images have width/height; hero is preloaded with high fetch priority; fonts `display: "swap"`.
5. Typing effect = staggered character opacity, never `width`.
6. Playwright motion lint uses `document.getAnimations()` keyframes **and** a stylesheet `@keyframes` scan (GSAP often skips the WAAPI).
7. Reduced-motion test: no `playState === "running"` except opacity-only.
8. Scroll LoAF: fail if any `long-animation-frame` has `blockingDuration > 50` or `duration > 100`.

## Budgets (source of truth: `performance-budgets.json`, mirrored in `BUDGETS.md`)

Mobile emulation, throttled: LCP ≤ 2.0s, CLS ≤ 0.02, TBT ≤ 150ms, initial JS ≤ 170 KB gzipped. Lighthouse Performance ≥ 95 mobile and ≥ 98 desktop. Accessibility = 100.

## Enforcement

Playwright motion lint, reduced-motion, and LoAF tests. LHCI assertions from the JSON. CI on every push and PR. Branch `demo/layout-animation-regression` animates `left` and is expected to fail; do not merge it.

## Workflow

M4 polish is done (MIT LICENSE, metadata/OG, skip-link, README deploy notes). After this milestone: `pnpm build` and tests, stop for review.

M3: assertions fail the build. Branch `demo/layout-animation-regression` is expected to fail CI; do not merge it.

Keep it small: no unused deps, small components, no dead code. Explain significant choices in 2–3 sentences. `docs/decisions.md` and `docs/case-study.md` are heading stubs only.

README must include: one-line pitch, `pnpm i && pnpm dev`, budgets table, how the gates work.
